---
// The Family Guide — the page someone lands on after enrolling, and the one
// they come back to later.
//
// ⚠️ PLACEHOLDER COPY. Every section below is holding wording pending Rob's
// approved family-guide draft. It is deliberately conservative: the safety
// section mirrors language already approved on /terms rather than making new
// claims, and the disaster paragraph is phrased as EFFORT, never as a
// guaranteed arrival — see docs/legal-source.md §4 item 8, open attorney items
// (b) and (c). `noindex` stays on until the real copy lands.
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT PERSONALIZED. This page is permanent and bookmarkable, so it
// is written to work for someone arriving cold months later. Passing a
// recipient's name through a query string would put a third party's name into
// browser history, shared links and referrer headers to buy a little warmth on
// one visit — the flow's no-third-party-data-in-URLs rule applies here too.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const SUPPORT_EMAIL = 'Mabel@AuntMabel.app';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your family guide · Aunt Mabel"
  description="Everything you'll want to know about your loved one's daily call from Aunt Mabel."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="wrap guide">
    <header class="guide-head">
      <p class="kicker">You're all set</p>
      <h1>Welcome to the family.</h1>
      <p class="guide-lede">
        Mabel will call your loved one at their chosen time, every day. Below is
        everything worth knowing — how to introduce her, what the calls are
        like, and how to reach us. Keep this page bookmarked; it's here whenever
        you need it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#talking">Talking to them about Mabel</a>
      <a href="#expect">What to expect</a>
      <a href="#safety">Important to know</a>
      <a href="#account">Your account</a>
    </nav>

    {/* ── 1 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="talking">
      <p class="section-num">One</p>
      <h2>How to talk to them about Aunt Mabel</h2>
      <p>
        This conversation goes better when it's framed as company rather than
        supervision. Most people don't want to be checked up on — but almost
        everyone likes being thought of.
      </p>
      <p>
        It helps to be straightforward that Mabel is an automated caller. People
        work it out quickly, and being told upfront lands far better than
        discovering it. Mabel will say so herself, gently, if she's ever asked.
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li><strong>Lead with the company, not the safety.</strong> "Someone friendly to talk to each day" sits better than "so we know you're okay."</li>
        <li><strong>Say it's automated.</strong> Plainly and early. It isn't a thing to work around.</li>
        <li><strong>Let it be theirs to end.</strong> Knowing they can stop it any time makes saying yes much easier.</li>
        <li><strong>Give it a couple of weeks.</strong> The first call is the strangest one. It gets comfortable quickly.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    {/* ── 2 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="expect">
      <p class="section-num">Two</p>
      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>
        Mabel calls at the same time each day. She's warm and unhurried — she
        asks how they slept, how they're feeling, what they've got on. It's a
        real conversation, not a checklist.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The first call is a little different.</strong> On it, Mabel will
        gently confirm they're happy to keep hearing from her. If they'd rather
        not, we stop right there and you aren't charged.
      </p>
      <p>
        If someone doesn't pick up, Mabel tries again later the same day. If she
        still can't reach them, we'll let you know.
      </p>
      <p>
        If anything in a conversation sounds concerning, we contact the people
        you named as emergency contacts — the same day, with what she heard.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* ── 3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="safety">
      <p class="section-num">Three</p>
      <h2>Important to know</h2>

      <div class="safety-callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Aunt Mabel is a friendly daily check-in — not an emergency,
          medical, or monitoring service.</strong> She is not a substitute for
          calling 911, and not a substitute for professional care.
        </p>
        <p class="safety-emergency">
          In an emergency, call <strong>911</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>Being plain about where the edges are:</p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li><strong>Mabel calls once a day.</strong> She isn't listening between calls, and she can't detect a fall or a medical event.</li>
        <li><strong>She won't call a doctor.</strong> If you gave us a doctor's details, we pass them along when we alert your contacts. We never call them ourselves.</li>
        <li><strong>She isn't medical advice.</strong> Mabel doesn't diagnose anything or weigh in on medication.</li>
        <li><strong>Alerts go to the people you named.</strong> If nobody is reachable, we can't escalate further on our own.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>When disaster strikes</h3>
      <p>
        When a disaster reaches your loved one's area, we ask our partner
        <strong>Cajun Navy Ground Force</strong> to make an in-person wellness
        check. Their teams are often already on the ground in affected
        communities.
      </p>
      <p class="honest-note">
        We want to be honest about what that is and isn't. It is a commitment to
        <strong>try</strong> — it is not a guarantee that someone will reach a
        particular door at a particular time. Disasters are chaotic, roads close,
        and demand can outstrip any team. Please don't treat the in-person check
        as a substitute for an evacuation plan.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* ── 4 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
    <section class="guide-section" id="account">
      <p class="section-num">Four</p>
      <h2>Your account, and how to cancel</h2>
      <p>
        Your first three days are free. After that it's $39 a month, and you can
        stop any time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cancelling is meant to be easy.</strong> Email us and we'll take
        care of it — no phone call, no retention conversation, no being passed
        around. If you cancel during the free trial, you're never charged at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        Changing the call time, updating a phone number, adding or swapping an
        emergency contact — email us for any of it and we'll sort it out.
      </p>

      <div class="contact-card-guide">
        <p class="contact-label">Talk to a person</p>
        <p class="contact-email">
          <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="contact-note">
          A real human reads these. If something's wrong with a call, say so —
          it's the fastest way to get it fixed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="guide-foot">
      Aunt Mabel is operated by Trustlight LLC. The in-person disaster check is
      carried out by our partner, Cajun Navy Ground Force.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide { max-width: 44rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }

  .guide-head { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .guide-head h1 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .guide-lede {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
    max-width: 40ch;
  }

  /* Quiet jump links — this page is long and people come back to it looking
     for one specific thing. */
  .guide-toc {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .guide-toc a {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--rose-deep);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .guide-toc a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--rose); }

  .guide-section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; scroll-margin-top: 2rem; }
  .section-num {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--rose);
  }
  .guide-section h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 1.95rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .guide-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.22rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .guide-section p {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    font-weight: 300;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .guide-section strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink); }

  .guide-list { margin: 1.25rem 0 1.5rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .guide-list li {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  /* Rose, not gold: this is the one part of the page that must read as a
     limit rather than a feature. */
  .safety-callout {
    padding: 22px 26px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rose);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--rose);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .safety-callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .safety-emergency {
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--rose-deep);
  }
  .safety-emergency strong { color: var(--rose-deep); font-weight: 600; }

  .honest-note {
    padding: 18px 22px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .contact-card-guide {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 20px;
  }
  .contact-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem !important;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
  }
  .contact-email {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem !important;
    font-family: var(--font-head);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .contact-email a { color: var(--rose-deep); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rose); }
  .contact-note { margin: 0 !important; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--soft-ink); }

  .guide-foot {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--soft-ink);
  }
</style>
